<title>AUSTRALIA: MIM says Q3 base metals output is lower.</title>
<headline>MIM says Q3 base metals output is lower.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mining house MIM Holdings Ltd said on Monday that base metals output in the third quarter ended March 31 was lower due to wet weather at Mount Isaaand operations elsewhere in the state of Queensland.</p>
<p>&quot;Production in all areas was impacted by extremely wet weather which resulted in extensive regional flooding and caused concentrate handling difficulties, humid conditions underground and electrical delays in major plant during January and February,&quot; MIM said.</p>
<p>It also said copper anode production was considerably reduced by a 25-day shutdown of the ISASMELT furnace.  </p>
